  <translations>
    <en>
      <description>Rain Bird 150-PGA-9V is a 1 1/2″ solenoid valve for higher-flow systems, equipped with a 9 V DC latching solenoid. It is designed for battery-powered controllers and allows irrigation zones to be controlled without 24 V wiring to the valve. Inline or angle installation is possible. PGA series operating pressure is up to about 10.4 bar.</description>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>b0</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>b00</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>150-PGA-9V</text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>b01</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text> — a 1″ diaphragm solenoid valve for automatic irrigation.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Purpose and operating principle</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The controller energises the solenoid, which operates the diaphragm and opens the water passage. When the signal stops, the valve closes automatically. The PGA series is a professional range with inline or angle installation, filtered pilot flow, slow closing and manual operation.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Construction and model-specific features</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The integrated flow-control handle adjusts delivery; internal manual operation simplifies service and slow closing helps reduce water-hammer risk. The 9 V DC latching solenoid requires a compatible battery controller and must not be connected to a 24 VAC output.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Hydraulic and electrical specifications</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>Size 1½″; operating pressure 1,04–10,4 bar; flow 30–100 GPM (6,81–22,70 m³/h); solenoid 9 V DC latching. Actual flow depends on pipe, filter and fitting losses as well as available pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Installation, adjustment and maintenance</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Connection: 1½″ female BSP thread. Before installation, confirm flow direction, operating pressure and thread standard. Fit the valve in an accessible valve box and flush the pipework before commissioning. During service, inspect the diaphragm, pilot filter, solenoid and seals. For flows below 2.27 m³/h, set the flow-control stem two full turns from fully open; below 1.14 m³/h, upstream filtration is recommended.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l0</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l00</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Check flow direction and stay within the permitted operating pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <level>1</level>
        <listItem>bullet</listItem>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Flush pipework before connection to keep sand and swarf out of the pilot circuit.</text>
        </children>
        <level>1</level>
        <listItem>bullet</listItem>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Leave access for future maintenance.</text>
        </children>
        <level>1</level>
        <listItem>bullet</listItem>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h5</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h50</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Choosing a compatible controller</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p5</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p50</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>This version uses a 9 V DC latching solenoid and requires a controller that supports this coil type. Do not connect it to a 24 VAC output.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p6</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p60</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Useful links: </text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>p61</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <marks>c</marks>
          <text>automatic irrigation controllers</text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>p62</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text> and </text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>p63</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <marks>s</marks>
          <text>valve installation and repair service</text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>p64</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>.</text>
